silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_07_worked_household_to_vetclinic_sections_02_revised_functorial_transport_concrete_anchor silm:hasExample "In 'RevisedFunctorialTransportConcreteAnchor', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, household-to-clinic.manifest.yaml with object assignment, arrow assignment, F1 and F2 witnesses, pullback constraints; also, the manifest field declaring clinic constraints pulled back to household checks; also, a derived anchor for the transport diagram: the clinic-side image of the household typed leg, carrying composition data.." .
